+   requirement to one primary check plus macOS/iOS/relay/review owner.
+4. Contract §§7–8 cover forked code, mutable actions, cache poisoning, artifact
+   substitution, tag spoofing, reruns, cancellation, concurrent releases,
+   compromised low-privilege credentials, and required rejecting fixtures at
+   named production call sites.
+5. Contract §9 records independent agent review and keeps human security,
+   release, and platform ratification at `TASK-260717-2d308k`; implementation
+   proceeds on the accepted draft while publication remains gated.
+
+## Reviewer evidence
+
+Pending independent agent verdict at the time this draft was created.
+
+## Residual risks
+
+- Workflows and branch protection are not implemented by this task; downstream
+  owners must prove every rejecting fixture and real call site.
+- Human governance ratification remains pending at `TASK-260717-2d308k` and is
+  required before publication, not before downstream implementation.
+- The requested `references/negative-evidence.md` is unavailable, so its
+  intended additional constraints remain unknown. Downstream negative evidence
+  obligations are explicit in contract §8.
